# The vibrator this device actually has.
#
# 🔴 Found 2026-08-19, once the vibrator HAL started running for the first time
# (its -stock rename had no exec type until today, so it never ran to be denied).
#
# There are TWO vibrator nodes here and MediaTek labels only the simple one:
#   sepolicy_vndr/basic/non_plat/genfs_contexts:268
#     /devices/platform/soc/soc:regulator_vibrator/leds/vibrator -> sysfs_vibrator
# Stock's HAL drives the other one -- an I2C AWINIC-class LRA at 0-0058, with
# f0/cali/lra_resistance/osc_cali/ram_update/rtp/gain, i.e. real haptics rather
# than a on/off motor -- and nothing labelled it, so it landed as plain sysfs:
#   avc: denied { read write } for comm="android.hardwar" name="activate"
#     scontext=u:r:hal_vibrator_default:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:sysfs:s0
#
# Only the LABEL is missing. MediaTek already grants the permission:
#   sepolicy_vndr/basic/non_plat/hal_vibrator_default.te
#     allow hal_vibrator_default sysfs_vibrator:file rw_file_perms;
# Confirmed live with chcon on the running device before this was written: the
# denials stopped and did not come back.
genfscon sysfs /devices/platform/soc/11e00000.i2c/i2c-0/0-0058/leds/vibrator_single u:object_r:sysfs_vibrator:s0
